{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PHASE 2 COMPLETE — fix pushed for review as Gerrit change 1395 (NOT closed; epic coordinator verifies).\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1395  (commit f078af4a65)\n\nTEST (RED -> GREEN, held out, with teeth)\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py — +244 lines, purely\nadditive (0 lines removed; no pre-existing test touched or weakened).\n\nRED first, for the RIGHT reason: 6 failed / 15 passed. The two pager cases failed with\n\"the pager made 26 calls against a startAt-ignoring server — it never self-terminated\n(offsets requested: [0, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 21, 24, 27]...)\", and all four fail-open cases\nwith \"DID NOT RAISE\" — the captured log showing our own error being absorbed into\n\"snapshot written without issuelink data (degraded)\". An initial run failed on a collection\nImportError, which is NOT a legitimate RED; the exception type (the oracle's contract\nsurface) was declared first so the RED came from behaviour.\n\nThe oracle was then MOVED OUT of the tree (git stash) before the fix subagent was launched;\nthe subagent got only the frozen contract card, never the test. On restore it was verified\nbyte-identical (diff clean — the fixer never touched it). GREEN: 21 passed, exit 0.\n\nMUTATION CHECKS (3, all returned the oracle to RED, fix restored after each)\n1. M1 re-introduced verbatim (pristine pre-fix loop restored): 3 failed / 18 passed —\n   exactly the pager + get_parent_map cases, at 26 calls. Negative controls stayed GREEN,\n   so the mutation is faithful. (A first, cruder excision left a dangling reference and went\n   red via NameError; that was discarded and redone as a verbatim revert.)\n2. M2 re-introduced (all four `except BackendPaginationStallError: raise` clauses deleted):\n   4 failed / 17 passed — each of the four fail-open sites caught individually.\n3. NEAR-MISS, the trap: adopt fetcher's short-page branch (`if len(batch) < page_size:\n   return out`) — the superficially plausible fix. 2 failed / 19 passed: the oracle REJECTS\n   it on the SHORT-page case. This is the strongest teeth evidence, since that branch is\n   exactly what copying `fetcher.py:335-345` would have produced.\n\nRefactoring litmus: every assertion is on observable behaviour (raised type, client call\ncount at the injected boundary, snapshot file contents, `__all__` membership — the latter\nbeing documented contract). No source-text greps, no private names. Renaming an internal\nin `_paged_search` breaks nothing.\n\nFIX (6 files; scope kept narrow for the parallel streams on 465d and set_parent)\n- `_backend.py` (+24) — `BackendPaginationStallError(RuntimeError)`. In CORE because\n  `fetcher` must name it and core must never import `adapters/`; an adapter-local error\n  would be unnameable at exactly the boundary that absorbs it.\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/_base.py` (+39) — the guard in `_paged_search`: track the\n  previous page's first key, raise on ANY repeat. Message names `startAt`, the stalled\n  offset, the repeated key and the JQL. Guarded against keyless/non-dict heads so two\n  consecutive keyless pages cannot fire a spurious `None == None` stall.\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/_hierarchy.py` (+10/-1) — the re-raise ahead of\n  `get_parent_map`'s broad clause. `set_parent` untouched.\n- `fetcher.py` (+25) — the re-raise ahead of all three `fetch_snapshot` enrichment\n  handlers. Import is module-level ABSOLUTE (a relative one breaks: this module is loaded\n  standalone via importlib in tests).\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py` (+9/-1) — facade re-export only, 2 effective\n  lines. No other change to the file 465d owns.\n- the test file above.\nAll files under the locked 800-line cap (fetcher.py is the closest at 771, was 746).\n\nGATES (real exit codes, captured directly — not piped through tail)\n- `make lint` -> 0   (first run was 2: ruff format on my new test block; fixed)\n- `make typecheck` -> 0\n- held-out oracle -> 0 (21 passed)\n- `pytest tests/unit` -> 8107 passed, 28 skipped, 1 error. The single error is a HARNESS\n  ARTIFACT OF THIS SESSION, not a regression: `test_lock_stale_reclaim.py::\n  test_acquire_does_not_reclaim_live_owner` guards against the repo HEAD moving mid-run,\n  and I committed the fix while the 22-minute suite was still running\n  (\"Test moved the repo HEAD (fc705c6441 -> f078af4a65)\"). Re-run with a stable HEAD:\n  24 passed, exit 0.\n- `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` -> OK, resolved 18a4-9df8-6373-4d9f.\n\nREPLICATION of the original report (the deciding evidence)\n- Report scenario (offset-blind DC): 26 calls, offsets [0,3,6,...] -> now 2 calls\n  [0, 3] and a named `BackendPaginationStallError`.\n- Fail-open swallow: `get_parent_map` returning a silent `{}` after 26 calls -> now the\n  error propagates (traceback through `_hierarchy.py:83` -> `_base.py:187`).\nThe original report no longer reproduces.\n\nSIBLING SWEEP (both axes)\nAxis 1 (construct) — exhaustive, not bounded: the whole reconciler contains exactly THREE\nunbounded loops (`grep -rn \"while True:\"`), and all three are the pagers already accounted\nfor: `fetcher.py:294` (guarded, bug deac), `_base.py:168` (this fix),\n`acli_graph.py:67` (guarded, bug cabc). There is no fourth instance.\nAxis 2 (parity) — one MISSING slot, fixed here. `_issues.py:262` / `acli.py:448` are N/A\n(single-page primitives, not pagers; the loop driving them is the guarded\n`fetcher._iter_pages`).\n\nRESIDUAL RISK — dispositioned\n1. TICKET FILED 9a46-1c90-5dd9-44e1 (linked discovered_from): Cloud's\n   `acli_graph.RunawayPaginationError` is swallowed by these SAME three fetcher handlers —\n   `grep -n \"RunawayPagination\" fetcher.py` returns NOTHING, so bug cabc's fix is itself\n   incomplete at the fetcher boundary. Proposed one-line fix recorded: subclass the new\n   core error. Not folded in — it changes CLOUD-surface behaviour, owned elsewhere.\n2. TICKET FILED 34c2-8c41-1a12-4254 (linked discovered_from): the structural guard\n   `test_no_search_issues_call_relies_on_the_default_page_size` has gone VACUOUS. It\n   AST-scans `transport.py` only, and 465d's split moved every `search_issues` call out —\n   MEASURED: 0 such calls remain in that file, so the guard passes unconditionally and\n   would not catch a fifth unpaginated caller. Notable because its sibling's own docstring\n   says \"a structural test that cannot fail is decoration\". Not fixed here: it is 465d\n   fallout and widening a guard's scope can surface unrelated offenders.\n3. ACCEPTED: `fetcher.py` is now 771/800 lines. Under the cap but the tightest headroom of\n   any file touched; the next addition there should split rather than append.\n\nSTALE CITATION corrected in the description: the ticket pointed at\n`adapters/jira/transport.py:379-416`; the pager now lives at\n`adapters/jira_datacenter/_base.py`.\n\nWorktree /Users/joeoakhart/18a4-stall is KEPT (unlanded change; needed to iterate on the\nGerrit gates). Gates LLM-Review / Verified were still pending at hand-off."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785885847758334001,"uuid":"2303f2c8-e77b-45e0-930a-599c917dada7"}